rationale: post-tool-use.js:39-45 and 59-66 verified. FG-M1-a722465e3b says editing dependency entries 'returns a reminder'; the designed predicate inspects only the replacement/content text, so an edit that deletes a PackageReference from a .csproj (empty new_string) gets no reminder although the manifest check (FG-M1-9ab7bbe4ae) still runs. Recorded as a trigger-boundary facet; it adds no agent obligation.
scenario: Edit replaces a PackageReference line in a .csproj with an empty string: manifest check runs, no add-dependency reminder; the same edit adding a PackageReference produces the reminder.
conf: HIGH
facet: FG-M1-a722465e3b | NEW_BEHAVIOR_BOUNDARY | For direct edits, the reminder fires only when the edit's new text (content, new_string or edits[].new_string) contains PackageReference, PackageVersion or a "dependencies"/"devDependencies" key, or the file is package.json; removal-only edits of .csproj/Directory.Packages.props entries get no reminder.

