@@ CIS-M1-U0011
disp: UNRESOLVED
nature: RECOMMENDED DEFAULT STRUCTURE ('useful default') with a permission (comments optional)
appl: actor=test author using dotnet-testing; action=use Arrange/Act/Assert; comments optional when phases are obvious; trigger=structuring NUnit tests; modality=UNCERTAIN (recommendation vs description); scope=dotnet-testing knowledge skill; exceptions=comments optional when phases are obvious; timing=standing; enforcement=none; loading=on-demand technique-only knowledge skill
compared: FG-M1-95e98f0dc1 FG-M1-b0eaad1b08 FG-M1-6ec961b701
rationale: dotnet-testing/SKILL.md:42-43 verified; no M1 group mentions AAA. Evidence points both ways: primary rejected it as permissive (ORPHAN-M1-0276), yet the M1 union registers comparable recommendation wording from the same skill ('a longer explicit case table is preferable', FG-M1-95e98f0dc1). Whether 'X is a useful default structure' is PREFER-strength guidance or a non-binding description is a normativity-threshold question that this review should not force; a wrong call would create an artificial representation difference.
scenario: A clear test that interleaves setup, actions and assertions: compliant if the sentence is descriptive, a deviation from a recommended default if it is guidance.
conf: LOW
question: Is 'Arrange / Act / Assert is a useful default structure; comments are optional when the phases are obvious' a registrable PREFER-strength recommendation, or permissive technique description?
next_check: Fix one Stage 2 normativity threshold for 'useful default' wording in technique-only knowledge skills and apply it identically to every candidate containing this sentence; if registrable, add it as a guidance clause anchored at dotnet-testing/SKILL.md:42-43.

@@ CIS-M1-0012
disp: EXISTING_GROUP_NEEDS_EXPLICIT_FACET
nature: RESPONSE CONTRACT (304 carries no normal representation)
appl: actor=agent implementing conditional HTTP responses; action=return 304 without the normal resource representation; trigger=conditional request whose cached representation is still valid; modality=MUST (contract of the status code, stated descriptively); scope=http-api knowledge skill; exceptions=none; timing=response generation; enforcement=none; loading=on-demand knowledge skill ('HTTP status-code reference and technique · Policy: rules/api.md, rules/error-handling.md')
match: FG-M1-43f86b8d6e
compared: FG-M1-8dc7ee59da
rationale: http-api/SKILL.md:87-89 verified. FG-M1-43f86b8d6e (primary MUST) cites exactly these lines and keeps 'only for conditional requests ... never a generic business response' but drops 'It carries no normal representation'. The 204 counterpart is registered as a body prohibition (FG-M1-8dc7ee59da), so the omitted sentence is a genuine part of the same 304 contract. Facet of the existing group; Codex NOVEL not confirmed as a distinct clause.
scenario: An endpoint correctly returns 304 for an unchanged ETag but serialises the resource body: FG-M1-43f86b8d6e is satisfied, the source contract is not.
conf: MEDIUM
facet: FG-M1-43f86b8d6e | NEW_BEHAVIOR_BOUNDARY | A 304 Not Modified response carries no normal representation (the resource body is not sent).
policy_hint: API-003 (Codex suggestion; not adjudicated)

@@ CIS-M1-U0012
disp: EXISTING_GROUP_NEEDS_EXPLICIT_FACET
nature: EXCEPTION to a DEFAULT (entities may be records when the model genuinely benefits)
appl: actor=agent using the modern-csharp knowledge skill; action=keep identity/lifecycle entities as classes unless the model genuinely benefits from record semantics; trigger=choosing class vs record for an entity; modality=DEFAULT with explicit exception; scope=modern-csharp knowledge skill ('Optional language technique'); exceptions=genuine benefit from record semantics; timing=design; enforcement=none; loading=on-demand knowledge skill
match: FG-M1-dd5a2d04c7
compared: FG-M1-c10790eb52
rationale: modern-csharp/SKILL.md:45-47 verified. FG-M1-dd5a2d04c7 (primary DEFAULT, exceptions 'none') cites lines 45-47 but omits the 'unless the model genuinely benefits' clause (protocol F6: exception inside the cited text, not stated). Under DEFAULT a justified deviation is already possible, so the explicit exception records granularity of the same rule rather than new allowed behaviour. Resolves the Codex question in favour of an explicit facet.
scenario: An identity-bearing model that demonstrably benefits from record semantics is written as a record: permitted by the source; the group text alone reads 'remain classes'.
conf: MEDIUM
facet: FG-M1-dd5a2d04c7 | NEW_GRANULARITY | Exception: an entity with identity and lifecycle may use record semantics when the model genuinely benefits from them.

