@@ CIS-M1-0014
disp: DISTINCT_UNREPRESENTED_CLAUSE
nature: WORKFLOW REVIEW STEP (investigation prompt of the supply-chain layer)
appl: actor=agent running the security-scan workflow; action=review unexpected or untrusted NuGet sources; trigger=security scan covering the .NET dependency/supply-chain layer; modality=PROCEDURAL (investigation prompt); scope=security-scan workflow via its private reference scan-layers.md; exceptions=irrelevant checks are skipped; prompts are not automatic vulnerability declarations; timing=during the scan; enforcement=instruction only; loading=private reference of a workflow skill, read during security scans
compared: FG-M1-71aa469282 FG-M1-77a9a56e68 FG-M1-e86e21ebbc FG-M1-be1a8db21a FG-M1-b8421aa55d
rationale: scan-layers.md:17-19 verified. Primary marked the sentence NON_NORMATIVE (EXC-015, the oracle's investigation-heuristics exclusion) and no M1 group mentions package sources; FG-M1-71aa469282 is the pre-install due-diligence rule, FG-M1-77a9a56e68 layer scope, the replica parts evidence discipline. The M1 union does register other scan-layer prompts as review duties (e.g. sanitizer-bypass review, debug-flag review), so by the union's own granularity this omitted prompt is an unrepresented procedural review step. The oracle exclusion is noted as context only.
scenario: A scan audits vulnerable packages and licences but never looks at a nuget.config pointing to an unexpected feed: no M1 group is violated, the scan procedure is.
conf: MEDIUM
open_issue: The same source sentence (scan-layers.md:17-19) also lists vulnerable direct/transitive dependencies, advisory severity, actual usage and patched compatible versions; apart from the CVSS/no-upgrade groups these do not appear in the M1 union. Outside this claim; not extracted here.
proposal: PROCEDURAL (review step) | security scan covering the .NET dependency and supply-chain layer | Review unexpected or untrusted NuGet sources as part of the dependency and supply-chain layer of a security scan.
policy_hint: EXC-015 context / WF-020 (non-binding)

@@ CIS-M1-0015
disp: DISTINCT_UNREPRESENTED_CLAUSE
nature: WORKFLOW REVIEW STEP (conditional lockfile review in the npm part of the supply-chain layer)
appl: actor=agent running the security-scan workflow; action=review lockfiles; trigger=npm frontend exists and package integrity or unexpected dependency changes are relevant; modality=PROCEDURAL, conditional; scope=security-scan workflow via scan-layers.md; exceptions=only when integrity/unexpected changes are relevant; timing=during the scan; enforcement=instruction only; loading=private reference of a workflow skill
compared: FG-M1-db44665d07 FG-M1-a90b921ef7 FG-M1-40154eacb3 FG-M1-bbd22299d0
rationale: scan-layers.md:25-29 verified. FG-M1-db44665d07 registers the production/development and direct/transitive distinctions of the same passage; lockfile groups (FG-M1-a90b921ef7 maintain and commit, FG-M1-40154eacb3 preserve during repair, FG-M1-bbd22299d0 missing-lockfile warning) concern maintenance, not inspection during a scan. The conditional review step is unrepresented.
scenario: An unexpected package change is investigated with npm audit and a manifest diff only; the lockfile's changed resolution/integrity entries are never reviewed.
conf: MEDIUM
proposal: PROCEDURAL (conditional review step) | security scan with an npm frontend where package integrity or unexpected dependency changes are relevant | Review the lockfiles when package integrity or unexpected dependency changes are relevant.
policy_hint: EXC-015 context / WF-020 (non-binding)
